 "footnotes": [
  "p. 3 n. 1 (on ut'a - à, line 14): The papyrus has [A1 G43 U28] (seated man first, then chick and fire-drill).",
  "p. 4 n. 1 (on ànt, first occurrence, line 15): In the Leyden Papyrus of [N29 N35 U15 N35 G1 A1] (Qenna; first sign a small triangle, coded N29, approximate) the corresponding passage has [D4 G1 G1 A1 N35 U23 D58 Y1a K1 O50:Q3 L1 D21 G43 D46:W11 G1 M17 M17 D4 A1 M17 K1:N35:X1 K1 Aa15 L1 D21 G43 O34]; we should then, probably add in the text of Ani after [M17 K1:N35:X1 K1], the words [Aa15 L1 D21 G43] \"in revolution.\" See Naville, Das aeg. Todtenbuch, Bl. xiv., ll. 13, 14.",
  "p. 4 n. 1 (raised mark after ba-à, line 18): a small raised stroke ' after the jabiru; no footnote text for it on the page (may be a stray mark or a second reference to n. 1)."
 ],
 "notes": "Range p.3 top to p.5 line 28 'Àusàr Ani'. Line in force at top of p.3 assumed 10 (first numeral on p.3 is 11.). Numerals printed inside words: 12. inside urt (before pavilion det), 19. inside setut - tu, 23. inside ṭātu - nà, 26. inside t'a (before boat det); such words keep the line in force at their start. No rubric overlines seen anywhere in pp.3-5 range. No square brackets in any hieroglyph line; [maa] p.4 l.17 is bracketed only in transliteration and its sign is printed faint/grey. Glosses for 'every day' (rā neb) and 'every place' (bu neb) given by meaning, not position. The tall L-shaped sign (àuset, se-ḥetem, Àusàr) coded Q1 throughout; the low runner with upcurled left end coded U15 (beḥen, seśep-à, Leyden footnote). The bevelled em sign Aa15 also writes m in χnem and se-ḥetem. Footnote p.3: lower edge of page also has signature 'B 2'."
}